# Dependencies are installed inside the image by `npm ci` against the
# lockfile. Copying the host's node_modules in would be slower, would ship
# whatever happens to be on one developer's laptop, and would be actively
# wrong: native modules compiled against macOS/arm64 do not run on
# alpine/musl. It also defeats the reproducibility npm ci exists to give.
node_modules

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Secrets. Configuration reaches the API as environment variables at run
# time (compose `env_file`), so a .env must never be baked into a layer --
# anyone who can pull the image can read its layers.
.env
.env.*

# VCS, editor and OS noise
.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store

# Build inputs and docs that the running app has no use for
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md

# init.sql belongs to Postgres, not to the API. Compose bind-mounts it
# straight into the database container's /docker-entrypoint-initdb.d, so it
# never needs to enter this image's build context.
db/

# Test and coverage artifacts, should any appear later
coverage
.nyc_output
